 "summary": "Not on 1h or 4h. Every Williams %R(14) setting there, long or short, landed inside the luck band. The result that holds up runs against the dip-buying idea: on daily candles, after %R(14) crossed up through −80, price fell 3.78% behind random entries 20 days later, and the result holds without its strongest stretch.",
 "verdicts": [
  {
   "use": "Buying the dip on 1h and 4h (below −80 or crossing up through it)",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "No better than random entries, whether as a level or as a cross back up through −80. This held on BTC, ETH and SOL alike."
  },
  {
   "use": "Buying the cross up through −80 on daily",
   "verdict": "worse",
   "text": "Price fell 3.78% behind random entries 20 days later. It holds without its strongest stretch and shows at 10 and 50 candles as well."
  },
  {
   "use": "Riding momentum on daily (crossing up through −20)",
   "verdict": "fragile",
   "text": "Beat random entries by 2.8%, but only because of SOL entries between Dec 29, 2020 and Jun 8, 2021. Without that stretch it is chance."
  },
  {
   "use": "Shorting overbought on daily (above −20 or crossing down through it)",
   "verdict": "fragile-worse",
   "text": "Worse than random, because price kept rising during single uptrend stretches. Without them it is chance, and on 1h and 4h these shorts showed nothing."
  }
 ],
 "notes": [
  "Holding a long while %R(14) was below −80 on 1h gave 24,641 entries in 2,641 separate moves. Twenty candles later they were 0.03% ahead of random entries, inside the luck band. The cross up through −80 enters less than half as often and landed at 0. On 4h both settings also sat inside the band.",
  "On daily, %R(14) crossing up through −80 gave 398 entries in 119 moves. Twenty days later they were 3.78% behind random entries. That holds without the stretch between Apr 13 and Jul 13, 2022, around the Terra collapse. It shows at 10 and 50 candles and fades to chance at 100. Split by regime, neither side clears its own band: 3.62% behind in uptrends and 1.89% behind in downtrends. The pooled result is not carried by one regime alone.",
  "The daily cross up through −20 beat random entries by 2.8%, but 25 entries between Dec 29, 2020 and Jun 8, 2021 carry it. Most of that is SOL, which was 7.32% ahead on its own with the same stretch behind it. In uptrends it was 2.85% ahead and also fragile. In downtrends it showed nothing.",
  "Daily shorts look bad only because of uptrend stretches. Shorting while %R(14) was above −20 did 3.73% worse than random, driven by 34 SOL entries between Jul 29 and Sep 9, 2021. The cross down through −20 did 2.84% worse, driven by the stretch between Dec 30, 2020 and Jun 11, 2021. Both are fragile-worse in uptrends and show nothing in downtrends.",
  "One regime split on 1h looks like a dip-buying edge and is not. In downtrends, %R(14) below −80 came out 0.08% ahead, but that rests on 10 entries on Jul 16, 2022. Without them it is chance, and it is chance at 10, 50 and 100 candles too.",
  "For a long DCA bot on 1h or 4h, %R(14) timing adds nothing on these pairs, so the DCA orders and take profit decide the result. On daily, the cross up through −80 came before further weakness more often than a bounce. That is a reason to leave it out of a daily long start condition, or to require a separate trend condition beside it. A daily short that opens on %R(14) above −20 traded against the strongest rallies."
 ],
